---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import TopBar from '../components/TopBar.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

const lastUpdated = '10 May 2026';
const businessEmail = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_BUSINESS_EMAIL || 'contact@shritaxi.com';
const businessPhone = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_BUSINESS_PHONE || '+916397321825';
---

<Base
  title="Terms & Conditions | Shri Taxi"
  description="Terms and conditions for booking taxi services with Shri Taxi in Dehradun and Uttarakhand — booking, pricing, cancellations, and liability."
  canonicalUrl="https://shritaxi.com/terms"
>
  <TopBar />
  <Header currentPath="/terms" />
  <main id="main-content">
    <section class="legal">
      <div class="container">
        <h1>Terms &amp; Conditions</h1>
        <p class="legal-meta">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

        <p>
          These Terms &amp; Conditions ("Terms") govern your use of Shri Taxi services and the website at
          <a href="https://shritaxi.com">shritaxi.com</a>. By making a booking with us — through the website,
          WhatsApp, phone, or any other channel — you agree to these Terms.
        </p>

        <h2>1. Service description</h2>
        <p>
          Shri Taxi provides on-demand taxi, airport transfer, outstation, hill-station and Char Dham Yatra
          services in Dehradun and across Uttarakhand. Vehicles range from sedans and SUVs to Innova Crysta and
          Tempo Travellers, supplied by us or by partner operators we work with.
        </p>

        <h2>2. Booking</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>A booking is confirmed only when we acknowledge it by phone, SMS, or WhatsApp with driver and vehicle details.</li>
          <li>Please share accurate trip details — pickup, drop, date, time, passenger count, and luggage. Incorrect details may lead to delays or revised pricing.</li>
          <li>You must be 18 or older to make a booking. You are responsible for the conduct of all passengers in your group.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>3. Pricing and payment</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Quoted fares are inclusive of driver allowance, fuel, and standard tolls unless stated otherwise.</li>
          <li>State entry permits, parking, and any extra night halts beyond the agreed itinerary are charged separately at actuals.</li>
          <li>Char Dham, snow-season, and festival-period trips may carry a seasonal surcharge that we communicate in writing before you confirm.</li>
          <li>Payments are settled directly with the driver — cash, UPI, GPay, PhonePe, Paytm, or bank transfer. We do not collect card payments online.</li>
          <li>An advance may be requested for multi-day trips and Char Dham packages. Any advance is adjusted in the final fare.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>4. Cancellation and refund</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Cancellations made more than 12 hours before the scheduled pickup are free of charge for local and short trips.</li>
          <li>For outstation and multi-day trips, cancellation within 24 hours of pickup may incur a charge to cover driver positioning and lost slots.</li>
          <li>For Char Dham and tour packages, the cancellation terms shared at the time of booking apply.</li>
          <li>Refunds of any advance, where due, are processed within 7 working days to the original payment method.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>5. Trip changes and waiting time</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Reasonable changes to the itinerary during the trip are accommodated where possible; significant route or distance changes may revise the fare.</li>
          <li>Waiting time beyond 30 minutes at pickup, or beyond the agreed schedule, may be charged at standard rates.</li>
          <li>Daily distance and hours included in tour packages are stated upfront; usage beyond those limits is billed at the per-km/hour rate disclosed at the time of booking.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>6. Vehicles and drivers</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>We allocate the vehicle category you booked. We may, with notice, substitute a vehicle of equal or higher category if the original is unavailable.</li>
          <li>All drivers carry valid commercial licences and the vehicle papers required by Indian and Uttarakhand transport regulations.</li>
          <li>Smoking, consumption of alcohol or illegal substances, and dangerous behaviour inside the vehicle are not permitted. Drivers may end the trip if safety is compromised.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>7. Luggage and personal belongings</h2>
        <p>
          Please confirm luggage volume in advance for compact vehicles. We are not liable for items left behind in
          the vehicle, but will make reasonable efforts to return them at the customer's cost.
        </p>

        <h2>8. Delays and force majeure</h2>
        <p>
          We aim to be on time, but we cannot guarantee arrival or journey times due to traffic, weather,
          landslides, road closures, vehicle breakdowns, regulatory checks, or other events outside our control. We
          are not liable for any indirect loss (such as missed flights, missed events, or onward bookings) caused by
          such delays. For airport pickups we recommend booking with a comfortable buffer.
        </p>

        <h2>9. Liability</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Vehicles operate under valid commercial insurance as required by law. Compensation for any incident is limited to that available under the applicable insurance.</li>
          <li>Our total liability for any claim relating to a booking is limited to the fare paid for that booking.</li>
          <li>We are not liable for any indirect, incidental, or consequential losses.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>10. Char Dham and high-altitude travel</h2>
        <p>
          Char Dham Yatra and high-altitude routes (Kedarnath, Badrinath, Auli, Chopta, etc.) involve mountain
          driving, weather risk, and physical exertion. Customers travel at their own risk and are responsible for
          assessing their own fitness, carrying necessary medication, and obtaining mandatory registrations and
          permits where required by the Government of Uttarakhand.
        </p>

        <h2>11. Website use</h2>
        <p>
          The content on shritaxi.com is provided for information. Fares, packages, and route details may change
          without notice. We do our best to keep the information accurate but do not warrant that it is error-free.
        </p>

        <h2>12. Governing law and disputes</h2>
        <p>
          These Terms are governed by the laws of India. Any dispute arising out of a booking shall be subject to
          the exclusive jurisdiction of the courts at Dehradun, Uttarakhand.
        </p>

        <h2>13. Changes to these Terms</h2>
        <p>
          We may revise these Terms at any time. The version in effect at the time of your booking is the version
          that applies to that booking.
        </p>

        <h2>14. Contact</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Phone: <a href={`tel:${businessPhone}`}>{businessPhone}</a></li>
          <li>Email: <a href={`mailto:${businessEmail}`}>{businessEmail}</a></li>
          <li>Address: Shri Taxi, Dehradun, Uttarakhand, India.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>

<style>
  .legal {
    padding: 80px 0 64px;
    background: var(--white);
  }
  .legal .container {
    max-width: 820px;
  }
  .legal h1 {
    font-size: 36px;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .legal h2 {
    font-size: 22px;
    margin: 32px 0 12px;
  }
  .legal p,
  .legal li {
    color: var(--slate);
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }
  .legal ul {
    padding-left: 20px;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }
  .legal a {
    color: var(--teal);
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
  .legal-meta {
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 14px;
    margin-bottom: 24px;
  }
</style>
